  "equipment_type": "Boiler controller",
  "applies_to": "AERCO boilers and water heaters with the C-More control on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the AERCO C-More control: 82 Analog Inputs, 17 polled by default. It reads unit status, outlet, inlet, outdoor, exhaust and FFWD temperatures, fire rate in/out, flame strength, O2 and CO, run hours and cycles, the fault log and the configuration values.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Aerco_C_More_Boiler_Controller_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the AERCO C-More Modbus register list (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/AercoCMore.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 17 of the 82 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
  ],
